WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:08.773
Google pitches Gemini 4 Argon for tougher coding and
longer tasks.

2
00:00:08.873 --> 00:00:13.262
Unveiled September thirtieth, it reached paid users on
October thirteenth.

3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:20.957
Its stable API accepts text, images, video, audio, and
PDFs, but returns text.

4
00:00:21.057 --> 00:00:25.404
A million-token shared budget includes input,
thinking, and output.

5
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:31.364
Google's eleven-hour coding case shipped two of six
proposals after review.

6
00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:36.707
That's promising for difficult work, but it also shows
why human checks still matter.

7
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.313
Independent rankings disagree.

8
00:00:40.413 --> 00:00:46.637
Argon leads Vals Index, while Artificial Analysis
ranks its high-effort setting eighth.

9
00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:49.249
Different tests answer different questions.

10
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.185
Early Reddit feedback is mixed.

11
00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:57.677
Some praise speed and security analysis; others report
architectural misses.

12
00:00:57.777 --> 00:01:00.396
These are anecdotes, not controlled tests.

13
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.697
Try it on a task with a clear finish line.

14
00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:07.461
Compare useful results, elapsed time, and total cost.

15
00:01:07.561 --> 00:01:10.905
Promising for hard work; keep the evidence in view.

